      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Can I add an address check to a Confirmation of Payee or Verification of Payee response?<svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9" /></svg></summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner"><p>Yes — ioNova ARS returns a sub-100ms address-quality verdict alongside your name/account match.</p></div></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">How big is the integration?<svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9" /></svg></summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner"><p>The smallest of any audience — one API group (Party Address, EP-01–07), pre-check only, no payment-message handling.</p></div></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">How fast is the check?<svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9" /></svg></summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner"><p>Sub-100ms via the structural PreCheck path.</p></div></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Do I have to process payment messages?<svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9" /></svg></summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner"><p>No — VOP/CoP providers use address-level endpoints only and never touch a pain or pacs message.</p></div></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Which tier fits?<svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9" /></svg></summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner"><p>Business or Corporate tier (data-scope only).</p></div></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">How quickly can we go live?<svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9" /></svg></summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner"><p>Typically days — a single REST integration into your existing response path.</p></div></div>
      </details>
